      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the mysterious case of the Jenkins ghost! In the world of containerized environments, these phantoms are often the result of resource contention or network issues. It's like a mischievous goblin playing hide and seek with your build process. Perhaps the goblin is hoarding resources, causing your build to vanish mid-execution. Or maybe it's playing tricks with the network, causing intermittent failures that are as elusive as a shadow in the moonlight.\n\nTo exorcise these phantom failures, you might want to consider the following steps:\n\n1. Check your container resources: Make sure your containers have enough CPU and memory allocated. A resource-starved container can behave like a goblin in a bottle, causing unexpected behavior.\n\n2. Inspect your network: Ensure that your containers have proper network access. A network issue can cause your build process to vanish, just like a goblin disappearing into thin air.\n\n3. Review your logs: Look for any clues in your logs that might point to the cause of the phantom failures. It's like trying to track down a mischievous goblin by following its footprints.\n\n4. Consider running your builds in parallel: Running your builds in parallel can help you identify if the phantom failures are caused by resource contention",
      "source": "target",
